        <p>Worth Monthly I - 7/51:</p>
        <p>PUBLIC AMUSEMENTS.</p>
        <p>ROYAL COURT THEATRE. " The Kelly Gang." ' This play, dealing with the adventures' gang of Australian Bushrangers, is a "thvilll and that is all. Ultra sensationalism served in a crude fashion, appeals to some people, at the Royal Court Theatre this week thef it with interest. The story is soon told., gentleman desperado is in love with 12 owner's daughter, and in his flight frail police he has many narrow escapes, which I vide the necessary thrills—of course, not for ting the super-abundance of shooting. David C. Noble, as the leader of the gang, Kelly, is a powerful actor, and carries the et ence away with his dashing, dare-devil noel As his "pals," Mr. Hal Howells and Mr. Fr. Allen are also good, whilst an impressive personation of the traitor, Skillian, is given Mr. Victor Vernon.</p>
